---
// The splash page. The documentation pages come from docs/ through Starlight.
import "../styles/splash.css";
import Logo from "@brand/logo.svg";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Svalbard is an open-source database backup CLI written in Rust. It backs up PostgreSQL and MySQL to S3, R2, SFTP and SCP."
    />
    <title>Svalbard</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <script>
      import "../scripts/app.mjs";
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header>
      <h1>
        <a class="brand" href="/"><Logo aria-hidden="true" />svalbard</a>
      </h1>
      <nav aria-label="Main">
        <a href="/docs/">Documentation</a
        ><a href="https://github.com/paulrose/svalbard">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="scene" aria-label="Illustration of a backup run">
        <canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <div class="labels" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="label trigger" data-anchor="trigger">
            <span class="name" data-text="trigger">cron</span
            ><span class="detail" data-text="schedule">0 2 * * *</span
            ><span class="state" data-text="clock">01:59:57</span>
          </p>
          <p class="label" data-anchor="database">
            <span class="name" data-text="database">PostgreSQL</span
            ><span class="state" data-text="snapshot"></span>
          </p>
          <p class="label" data-anchor="svalbard">
            <span class="name">svalbard</span
            ><span class="state" data-text="svalbard"></span>
          </p>
          <p class="label" data-anchor="storage">
            <span class="name" data-text="storage">Amazon S3</span
            ><span class="state" data-text="stored"></span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <noscript
          ><p class="no-script">
            A scheduled job starts Svalbard. It copies the database from a
            snapshot, closes the snapshot, then uploads the backup to storage.
          </p></noscript
        >
        <p class="sr-only">
          A cron job or scheduled CI workflow starts Svalbard. Svalbard opens a
          snapshot of a PostgreSQL or MySQL database and writes a backup from
          it. The snapshot closes. Only then does Svalbard upload the backup to
          storage, where it settles beside earlier backups.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="intro">
        <p>
          Svalbard is an open-source database backup CLI, written in Rust. It
          dumps the database from a snapshot, closes the snapshot, and only then
          uploads the backup.
        </p>
        <p class="adapters">
          PostgreSQL, MySQL <span aria-hidden="true">→</span
          ><span class="sr-only">to</span> Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, SFTP, SCP
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="docs" id="docs" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
        <h2 id="docs-title">Documentation</h2>
        <div>
          <pre><code>svalbard config check --config svalbard.toml
svalbard backup --config svalbard.toml --json</code></pre>
          <ul class="contents">
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/install/"><span>Install</span><span>The release archive and the native clients</span></a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/configuration/"><span>Configuration</span><span>Files and environment variables, secrets from CI</span></a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/ci/"><span>Run in CI</span><span>CI jobs, schedules and a GitHub Action</span></a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/database-safety/"><span>Databases</span><span>PostgreSQL and MySQL, snapshots and locks</span></a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/storage/"><span>Storage</span><span>Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, SFTP and SCP</span></a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/docs/restore/"><span>Restore</span><span>Back into a database with the native clients</span></a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
        <h2 id="origin-title">The name</h2>
        <p>
          Svalbard is an Arctic archipelago. Near Longyearbyen, the
          <a href="https://www.seedvault.no/">Svalbard Global Seed Vault</a>
          keeps duplicate seed samples from gene banks around the world, so
          their collections can be rebuilt if the originals are lost. In 2015,
          the research centre ICARDA made the first withdrawal, to rebuild
          collections that the war in Syria had cut off. The project takes its
          name from the islands and the vault.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/paulrose/svalbard/blob/main/LICENSE"
          >MIT License</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Colours follow daylight in Longyearbyen:
        <span data-daylight>Longyearbyen, Svalbard</span>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
